      },
      "speakerLabel": "OLD MAN.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "macbeth/sceneII_20.4/p@57023",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "ROSS.\nAnd Duncan’s horses (a thing most strange and certain)\nBeauteous and swift, the minions of their race,\nTurn’d wild in nature, broke their stalls, flung out,\nContending ’gainst obedience, as they would make\nWar with mankind.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
